# PLACEHOLDER ONLY. A real secrets.env.enc is an ansible-vault (or sops)
# ENCRYPTED blob, never plaintext like this. This file exists so the example
# layout is complete; it is read as-is only because SECRETS_METHOD=none in
# this example's instance.env, which is for local/dev use only.
#
# To create the real thing:
#   ansible-vault encrypt --vault-password-file <password-file> secrets.env.enc
#
# Content before encryption, flat KEY=value, one credential per line, e.g.:
#   EXAMPLE_API_KEY=replace-me
